  <div style="width: 80%; margin: 0 auto">
    <& /page/page_title.mas, title => '一項以番茄為模式系統編目並研究細胞壁蛋白質組（分泌蛋白質組）動態特性的專案(A project to catalog and study the dynamic properties of the cell wall proteome (the secretome), using tomato as a model system.)' &>
  </div>

  <div id="secretom_summary" style="float: left; width: 50%">
    <&| /page/info_section.mas, title => '摘要(Summary)' &>

      <p>
      <a class="info_link" href="/secretom/detail/cell_wall">植物細胞壁／質外體(plant cell wall/apoplast)</a> 在生長、發育以及對環境條件和病原體與昆蟲侵襲的反應等諸多方面發揮著基礎性作用(plays a fundamental role in many aspects of growth, development, and responses to environmental conditions and assault by pathogens and insects)。因此，植物蛋白質組的相當大部分定域於細胞壁／質外體中並不令人意外(It is therefore not surprising that a substantial portion of the plant proteome is localized in the cell wall/apoplast)。然而，儘管目前正在進行主要倡議以繪製許多植物細胞器的蛋白質組圖譜（例如 <a  href="http://ppdb.tc.cornell.edu/dbsearch/subproteome.aspx">
      葉綠體(chloroplast)</a>），但相較於其他亞細胞區室，細胞壁蛋白質組或「分泌蛋白質組（secretome）」的特徵分析要少得多(the cell wall proteome, or "secretome", is far less well characterized than those of other subcellular compartments)。
      </p>

      <img width="250" style="display: block; margin: 0 auto" src="/img/secretom/proteome.png" />

      <p>
      <strong>什麼是「分泌蛋白質組」？(What is the "secretome"?)</strong> 「分泌蛋白質組（secretome）」一詞通常用於指分泌到細胞質膜外的蛋白質群體，但也可以用來描述進入 <a href="/secretom/detail/secretion_path">分泌途徑(secretory pathway)</a> 的蛋白質組子集(The term "secretome" is generally used to refer to the population of proteins that are secreted outside the plasma membrane of a cell, but can also be used to describe the subset of the proteome that enter the secretory pathway)。
      </p>

      <p>
      <strong>此項由 NSF 資助的專案之目的(The purpose of this NSF-funded project)</strong> 是以番茄（<i>Solanum lycopersicum</i>）為模式系統，編目並研究細胞壁蛋白質組（或分泌蛋白質組）的動態特性(is to catalog and study the dynamic properties of the cell wall proteome, or secretome, using tomato (Solanum lycopersicum) as a model system)。
      </p>


      <p>
      <strong>為什麼要研究「分泌蛋白質組」？(Why study the "secretome"?)</strong> 細胞區室的蛋白質組分析揭示了特定蛋白質或蛋白質複合物的亞細胞定位，這進而成為理解蛋白質功能的寶貴步驟(Proteomic analysis of cellular compartments reveals the subcellular locations of a specific protein, or protein complex, which in turn can be a valuable step towards understanding protein function)。定位資訊亦有助於鑑定蛋白質交互作用和標靶途徑，以及引導蛋白質至不同細胞位置的胜肽基序和結構標籤(Localization information also helps in the identification of protein interactions and targeting pathways, and peptide motifs and structural signatures that can direct proteins to various cellular locations)。此外，亞細胞蛋白質組的分析具有需要「生物學預分級分離」的優勢，這可大幅提高低豐度蛋白質的檢測率(In addition the analysis of a subcellular proteome has the advantage of requiring "biological pre-fractionation," which can substantially enhance the detection of lower-abundance proteins)。
      </p>

    </&>
  </div>
  <div style="float: right; width: 50%">

